      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Nonspecific low back pain (LBP) is very common and the economic impact of absenteeism has not been completely established in Spain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHOD",
          "content": "We have valued LBP and the cost of worker's compensation in Spain with the available information between 1993-1997."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The mean LBP was 55,388 per year (SD 9,230.1). The transitory LBP disability was 21.9 days, with a range between 19.7 and 24.2 days. The total cost of worker's compensation LBP claims was 11,000 million pesetas/year, and the mean cost by worker was 209,666 pesetas/year."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The worker's compensation LBP claims was higher in Spain that in the European Union."
        }
      ]},
